  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shri Manjunath Shakar Shetty vs The State Of Karnataka on 13 February, 2024 Author: N.S.Sanjay Gowda Bench: N.S.Sanjay Gowda -1- Nc: 2024:Khc-D:3445 Crl.P No. 102338 of 2023 In The High Court Of Karnataka, Dharwad Bench Dated This The 13Th Day Of February, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr Justice N.S.Sanjay Gowda Criminal Petition No.102338 Of 2023 Between: Shri Manjunath Shankar Shetty, Age. 56 Years, Occ. Business, R/O. Sadashivalli, Targod, Tq. Sirsi, Dist. Uttara Kannada, Pin-581402. ... Petitioner (By Shri. Rakesh S. Hattikatagi, Advocate) And: The State Of Karnataka, By Food Safety Officer, Office Of Taluka Health Officer, Sirsi, R/By The State Public Prosecutor, Digitally High Court Of Karnataka, signed by Manjanna Manjanna E E Date: Dharwad Bench. ... Respondent 2024.02.17 Shri Manjunath Shakar Shetty vs The State Of Karnataka on 13 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/78514232/ 1 10:55:52 +0530 (By Shri. P.N. Hatti, Hcgp) This Criminal Petition Is Filed U/Sec. 482 Of Cr.P.C. Seeking To Allow The Petition And Quash Entire Proceedings In Cc No.702/2020 (Arising Out Of Private Complaint No.115/2020) At Annexure-A Pending Before Ii Addl. Jmfc Court, Sirsi For The Alleged Offence P/U/S 59(i) Of Food Safety And Standards Act, To Meet The Ends Of Justice. This Petition, Coming On For Admission, This Day, The Court Made The Following: -2- Nc: 2024:Khc-D:3445 Crl.P No. 102338 of 2023 Order",
    "facts": "1. This petition is filed challenging the initiation of the criminal proceedings for commission of an alleged offence under Section 59(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (\"the Act\" for short). The Form-B, which is produced Annexure-D indicates that the sample was received by the designated Officer on 24.07.2019 for analysis and the same was analyzed between 05.08.2019 and 08.08.2019 and thereafter, the report was stated to have been prepared on 08.08.2019 itself. 3.",
    "arguments": "2. It is the specific contention of the petitioner that the statutory rule requires that the report of the Food Analyst be dispatched within 14 days.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. It is the specific contention of the petitioner that the statutory rule requires that the report of the Food Analyst be dispatched within 14 days.",
